{
  // Trainers (phase 5.1): the trainer of a run gives a passive and an active ability, and shows in the HUD's card.
  // "passive": always-on "modifiers" (the same fields as an item's "perLevel"; fractions: 0.1 = +10%) and "typePower",
  // extra damage of the moves of the trainer's "type".
  // "active": one of ten archetypes (phase 5.2), on the Q key with "cooldown" seconds between uses:
  //   Shield      blocks the next "charges" hits within "duration" s
  //   Heal        heals "power" of the max PS at once
  //   Wave        a ring within "radius" px: regular enemies lose "power" of their max PS (Dominanti and boss a tenth) and fly back
  //   SlowTime    enemies and their shots move at "power" of their speed for "duration" s
  //   Intangible  no hit lands for "duration" s
  //   TypeBoost   moves of the trainer's type deal "power" more for "duration" s, the others a third of it (all of them without a type)
  //   Fortune     every gem flies in; experience and coins grow by "power" for "duration" s
  //   Frenzy      move cooldowns shrink by "power" for "duration" s
  //   StatusStorm every enemy on screen catches "status" with chance "power" (immunities and resistances apply)
  //   Haste       the player runs "power" faster for "duration" s
  // "unlock": Start (Ash), Defeat (beat them at Ultra in their challenge, phase 5.3), Mission or Shop (with "price").
  // The portrait is content/trainers/<sprite>.png ("sprite" defaults to the id).
  // "team" (phase 5.3): the Pokémon of their challenge, in the order they come out; the last one is the ace.
  "version": 1,

  // Phase 5.3: a challenge run ends with the trainer instead of the level's boss. Their Pokémon come out one at a time,
  // "nextDelay" seconds after the previous one faints, each a boss fighting like "member" (the ace like "ace"); "hp"
  // multiplies its PS on top of the level's growth, as for the level's boss (Pinsir has 60). Phase 5.3: first 22 and 34; a gym team lasted about 165 s (Pinsir about 70), now about a third less. Volleys shoot the move of
  // "shots" for the Pokémon's first type; Rock and Ground, with no move there, throw rocks instead.
